<LegalLayout
  pageTitle="Privacy · Pro Se Fair Play Mediation"
  description="How Pro Se Fair Play Mediation handles privacy and security — confidentiality of mediation sessions and infrastructure-level protections for the website."
  title="Privacy &amp;"
  titleItalic="Confidentiality"
  lede="How your mediation, your communications, and your data are kept private — both in session and in transit."
>
      <h2 class="display section-h2">Confidentiality of Mediation</h2>
      <p>
        Mediation is private. Discussions, negotiations, and potential
        resolutions remain confidential, unlike court proceedings which
        are part of the public record.
      </p>
      <p>
        Confidentiality in Florida mediation is defined by Chapter
        44 of the Florida Statutes and the Florida Supreme Court Rules
        for Certified and Court-Appointed Mediators. Anything shared with
        the mediator in session, except in narrow circumstances required
        by law, stays in the room. See Florida Statutes 44.406 and 44.407.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display section-h2">Website Security</h2>
      <p>
        This website is hosted on Cloudflare's global network, which
        provides several layers of security.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>HTTPS encryption everywhere</strong> — all traffic
          between your browser and this site is encrypted with TLS, with
          certificates auto-renewed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No personal data stored on the website itself</strong>
          — there is no database, and nothing to be stolen.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        That said, no internet transmission can be guaranteed 100% secure.
        Information you share with me through any online channel is shared
        at your own risk, with reasonable industry-standard protections
        in place.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display section-h2">Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        We collect only the information you provide voluntarily:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Information submitted when booking a consultation (name, email, phone, brief description of your situation, conflict-check details)</li>
        <li>Email correspondence you initiate with me</li>
        <li>Information you enter in the "keep me posted" form on this site (first name, email, an optional mobile number, a rough timeframe, and an optional one-line note about what your inquiry concerns)</li>
        <li>Standard server logs (IP address, browser type) for security and routine operation</li>
        <li>If you arrived from an online advertisement, the identifier Google places in the link you clicked, together with any campaign labels in it. This is kept in your browser for up to 90 days and, if you later submit the form, is stored with your inquiry so that I can tell which advertising is worth paying for. It is not used to build a profile of you and is not shared with anyone other than the providers described below.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I do not sell your information. I do not share it with third
        parties except as necessary to provide my services such as scheduling and payment processing.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display section-h2">How Inquiries Are Handled</h2>
      <p>
        Inquiries sent through this website are held in a client relationship
        management system so that I can follow up with you. To route an inquiry
        to the right response, the information you submit through the form may
        be processed by service providers acting on my behalf, including an
        automation service and an artificial intelligence service that reads
        your one-line note in order to categorize the inquiry and to identify
        matters that should reach me personally rather than receive an
        automated reply.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Text messages.</strong> If you give a mobile number and tick the
        box beside it, an automated text acknowledging your inquiry is sent to
        that number, with a link to book a consultation. That box is the only thing
        that authorizes a text: a number given without it is used for a phone
        call and is never texted. You can reply STOP to any message and no
        further texts will be sent. Message and data rates may apply, and the
        message is delivered through a messaging provider acting on my behalf.
      </p>
      <p>
        These providers process the information to deliver that service and are
        not permitted to use it for their own purposes. The information used
        for this is limited to what the form collects. Please do not describe
        your situation in detail on a web form; it is not a confidential
        channel, and it is not needed in order to reach me.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>This applies to inquiries only.</strong> Once mediation is
        under way, communications made in the course of that mediation are
        confidential and privileged under section 44.405, Florida Statutes.
        Nothing about the substance of a mediation is placed into an automation
        service or an artificial intelligence service.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can ask at any time what information is held about you, or ask for
        it to be deleted, by emailing
        <a href="mailto:info@prosefairplaymediation.com">info@prosefairplaymediation.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display section-h2">Questions</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about privacy or how your information is handled,
        email <a href="mailto:info@prosefairplaymediation.com">info@prosefairplaymediation.com</a>.
      </p>
</LegalLayout>
